+### Variable-size results and partial reads
+
+Pass `growable: true` when result sizes vary per request. `byteLength` is then the initial slot
+capacity, and `tryAcquire({byteLength})` / `acquire({byteLength})` reserve a slot that holds the
+request: the smallest idle slot that fits is reused, otherwise an idle slot is replaced by a
+larger one (rounded up to a power of two). A warm ring does not allocate. Without `growable`, a
+request above `byteLength` throws.
+
+When the useful length of a capacity-sized result is written by the GPU itself (a counter followed
+by that many records), `ticket.readPartial({headerByteLength, getByteLength})` maps the header,
+asks `getByteLength(header)` how much of the encoded range is used, and maps only that prefix. The
+bytes past the used length are copied on the GPU but never mapped.
+
+```ts
+const ring = new GPUReadbackRing(device, {byteLength: 1024, slotCount: 3, growable: true});
+const ticket = ring.tryAcquire({byteLength: results.byteLength});
+if (ticket) {
+  ticket.copyFrom(commandEncoder, results);
+  device.submit(commandEncoder.finish());
+  const {data} = await ticket.readPartial({
+    headerByteLength: 4,
+    getByteLength: header => 4 + new Uint32Array(header.buffer)[0] * 16
+  });
+}
+```
+
 ### Backpressure, cancellation, and loss
 
 An unused reservation can be cancelled immediately. Once a copy is encoded, its destination cannot
